 owner that call sites resolve at call time, so the migrated tests still observe the patch.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["reconcile.py:61-65: '...bind their names at module level so (a) the staying phase helpers call them as bare names — preserving the monkeypatch seam tests rely on — and (b) attribute access (reconcile.<name>) keeps resolving...'","reconcile.py:98-103: 'Bound as a MODULE attribute reconcile.compose_reconciler_runtime ... so tests can monkeypatch this exact attribute.'","Rubric G6(1): hidden ordering/binding assumption — an import-time-frozen alias means a monkeypatch on the new owner is not seen unless call sites resolve the owner dynamically."],"finding":"The reconcile.py pass-helper/runtime bindings are not merely passive re-exports: the module's own staying phase helpers (`_persist_and_log`, `reconcile_once`) call them as module-level BARE NAMES, and tests monkeypatch `reconcile.<name>` relying on that exact bare-name resolution as the seam (see the explicit comment at reconcile.py:61-65 and :91-103). The plan says to migrate monkeypatch consumers to the canonical owner but does not address that the in-reconcile.py bare-name call sites are the same bindings, so removing them requires the call sites to reference the canonical owner AT CALL TIME (not an import-frozen alias) or the migrated monkeypatch seam will no longer be observed by the running code path.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fffcffb0415289b4e","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Scope ('reconciler pass-helper/runtime re-exports')","norm_id":"nf261f5a4b7742446","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A test monkeypatches the canonical owner but the reconcile phase helper still calls a stale bare name bound at import time -> test exercises unpatched code and passes against the wrong binding.","Monkeypatch is migrated to owner module but reconcile_once/_persist_and_log call sites are not repointed -> production/prod path diverges from what tests patch."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Enumerate the specific reconcile.py re-exported names in scope and state that their bare-name call sites in the reconcile spine (_persist_and_log, reconcile_once, _advance_baselines) will be rewritten to the canonical owner, not merely deleted.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2812,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["reconcile.py:62-65 'the staying phase helpers call them as bare names — preserving the monkeypatch seam tests rely on'","reconcile.py:84-85 're-bound here so the bare-name calls in _persist_and_log and the reconcile._advance_baselines import in the A3 oracle both keep resolving'","reconcile.py:92-93 're-bound here so reconcile_once calls them as bare names'"],"finding":"The plan characterizes the reconcile.py pass-helper/runtime re-exports as 'forwarding bindings [that] retain a second owner', but reconcile.py's own comments (lines 62-65, 84-85, 92-93) state these module-level bindings exist so the reconcile spine's phase helpers (_persist_and_log, reconcile_once) invoke them as BARE NAMES. Removing the bindings therefore requires rewriting those bare-name call sites (or importing from reconcile_helpers), not merely deleting a re-export. The scope treats them as pure shims and does not enumerate WHICH of the ~20 names (StatusMappingError, preflight_status_mapping, _commit_binding_store_snapshot, _read_local_tickets, ensure_selection_current, narrow_selection_inputs, _build_filter_target_set, _mutation_matches_filter, _build_plan_entries, _NoOpSyncLogger, _write_prev_snapshot_key_set, _accepts_*, _advance_*, _write_facade_enabled, _resolve_pass_transport, bind_operation_runtime, compose_reconciler_runtime) are in scope.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f52017acd2f0fd772","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope: 'reconciler pass-helper/runtime re-exports'; Context/Problem: 'reconcile forwards listed pass helpers'","norm_id":"n107e4210ad04a663","priority":0.4188,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor deletes a re-export binding and the reconcile spine's bare-name call raises NameError at runtime","Reviewer cannot confirm the edit set is complete because the specific bindings are never listed"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"List each re-bound name from reconcile.py:70-106 and, for each, name the in-module caller that must switch to the reconcile_helpers/pass_support/runtime import so no bare-name call is orphaned.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows